				<div class="info">
					<span class="printuser avatarhover"><a href="http://www.wikidot.com/user:info/cryonicautumn" onclick="WIKIDOT.page.listeners.userInfo(4899605); return false;"  ><img class="small" src="http://www.wikidot.com/avatar.php?userid=4899605&amp;amp;size=small&amp;amp;timestamp=1608238263" alt="CryonicAutumn" style="background-image:url(http://www.wikidot.com/userkarma.php?u=4899605)"/></a><a href="http://www.wikidot.com/user:info/cryonicautumn" onclick="WIKIDOT.page.listeners.userInfo(4899605); return false;" >CryonicAutumn</a></span> <span class="odate time_1555121855 format_%25e%20%25b%20%25Y%2C%20%25H%3A%25M%7Cagohover">13 Apr 2019 02:17</span>
														</div>
			</div>
			<div class="content" id="post-content-4217387">
									

<p>Thanks go to GenericSkipper, N_AEpic_Fael, Calamitous1, amazingfantasy, crashington, 301320290, Zyn, and justeago for critique. Additional thanks go to Voct for sending me <a href="https://www.redbubble.com/people/lgracebo/works/34934574-i-eat-oil-paintings?cat_context=u-tees&amp;grid_pos=5&amp;p=classic-tee&amp;rbs=7607866b-768e-435c-a7f8-582e84d23179&amp;ref=shop_grid&amp;searchTerm=museums%20t-shirts" target="_blank">this</a> over IRC in response to my draft.</p>
<div class="collapsible-block">
<div class="collapsible-block-folded"><a class="collapsible-block-link" href="javascript:;">+&nbsp;Deep&nbsp;author&nbsp;commentary</a></div>
<div class="collapsible-block-unfolded" style="display:none">
<div class="collapsible-block-unfolded-link"><a class="collapsible-block-link" href="javascript:;">-&nbsp;Close</a></div>
<div class="collapsible-block-content">
<p>I have no idea how this popped up in my head. I just remember thinking &quot;A YouTube food reviewer: but they eat priceless masterpieces.&quot; Naturally, it spiraled a little out of control and this ended up being written.</p>
<p>The original draft for this was off the walls silly. However, I ended up getting a different image in my head of 4272's character along this time. I ended up actually&#8230; kind of respecting his worldview. Like, I don't condone destroying art, but when I was writing how he justifies it to himself, there was an aspect of &quot;this is my life, this is what I do&quot; that I can respect. The second draft ended with a somewhat edgy rant alluding to an aspect of 4272's backstory where he snapped and hurt the kids who bullied him. This didn't end up working well for his character, so I switched it to an accidental, but still angry action brought through poor control of his teleportation. There's some other stuff there to be unpacked, but I don't want to do a death of the author thing and tell-alls kinda ruin the point of having subtle clues.</p>
</div>
<div class="collapsible-block-unfolded-link"><a class="collapsible-block-link" href="javascript:;">-&nbsp;Close</a></div>
</div>
</div>

